          <div class="msv__process-step-num">3</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Book Cita Previa</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">4</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Submit Application</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">5</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Provide Biometrics</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">6</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Collect New TIE</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Detailed Steps</h3>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 1: Check Your Eligibility Window</h4>
        <p>Look at your current TIE card. Identify the expiration date. You are eligible to apply from 60 days before this date. Mark your calendar. Set a reminder for 75 days before expiry to stay ahead of cita previa demand.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 2: Gather All Required Documents</h4>
        <p>Document requirements vary by visa type (see section below). Core documents include: passport, current TIE card, empadronamiento, proof of income/savings, health insurance, accommodation proof, and completed EX-09 form. Organize these before booking your appointment.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 3: Book Your Cita Previa</h4>
        <p>Visit the provincial immigration office website (Delegación de Extranjería) or use the national system. Cita previa appointments fill quickly, especially near renewal deadlines. Book as soon as you enter the eligibility window. Some provinces allow online booking; others use in-person queues.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 4: Submit Your Application</h4>
        <p>At your cita previa, submit your completed application along with all required documents. The staff will verify everything is in order. If anything is missing, you may be asked to reschedule. Pay the €16.32 fee via Tasa 790-052.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 5: Provide Biometric Data</h4>
        <p>You will be scheduled for a biometric appointment (fingerprints, photograph) at the immigration office. This usually happens 1–2 weeks after your initial submission. Attend on time. This appointment is mandatory.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h4 style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Step 6: Collect Your New TIE Card</h4>
        <p>Once processing is complete (typically 30–60 days), you will be notified to collect your new TIE card from the immigration office. Bring your old card and a valid ID. Your new card is now valid for your renewal period (2 years for NLV renewal, 3 years for DNV, etc.).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DOCUMENTS REQUIRED -->
  <section class="msv__section--cream">
    <div class="msv__container">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Documents Required for Renewal</h2>
        <p>Every renewal requires core documents. Additional documents depend on your visa type.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Core Documents (All Applicants)</h3>
      <ul style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <li>Current TIE card (original)</li>
        <li>Valid passport (original + copy of data page)</li>
        <li>Completed EX-09 renewal form</li>
        <li>Proof of empadronamiento (municipal registration certificate)</li>
        <li>Health insurance documentation (valid during entire renewal period)</li>
        <li>Criminal background check (from home country, apostilled if required)</li>
        <li>Receipt of €16.32 fee payment (Tasa 790-052)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Financial & Housing Documents</h3>
      <ul style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <li>Proof of income or savings (bank statements, tax returns, employment contract)</li>
        <li>Proof of accommodation (lease, property deed, utility bill in your name)</li>
        <li>Tax registration number (NIE) documentation</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Visa-Type-Specific Documents</h3>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Non-Lucrative Visa:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Proof of passive income (~€2,300–€2,500/month minimum)</li>
          <li>Bank statements (last 3–6 months)</li>
          <li>No employment contract allowed</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Digital Nomad Visa:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Proof of remote work contract</li>
          <li>Bank statements showing freelance/remote income</li>
          <li>Professional certificates or client letters</li>
          <li>Tax return showing non-Spanish source income</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Student Visa:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Current enrollment certificate</li>
          <li>Proof of financial means (yourself or sponsor)</li>
          <li>Official transcript or academic record</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Work Permit:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Employment contract</li>
          <li>Employer sponsorship letter</li>
          <li>Tax withholding statements (últimos recibos de nómina)</li>
          <li>Social Security enrollment proof (afiliación)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

